  "details": "Currently there is no way to share a market place avatar out side of VRChat.\n\nHaving just a simple \"Change into avatar\" like you do if its a public or you own it, but instead switching you into the avatar Demo.\n\nThat, and or \"Open store page ingame\" button that does, well, opening the store page for the avatar in your vrchat game. Like when you click on a store page thing in a world to bring up a group or world store, but again, triggered via the website.\n\nThis way you can share the avatar link, they can view all the information on the avatar, and then try on the avatar ingame via the site, that way they can try it out, and view the avatar ingame to view the actual store page where they can buy it.\n\nThis means creators can also link the avatar within their communities, especially if Marketplace exclusive and not being sold in any other out of VRC stores.\n\nThis way its not as tedious to add the whole purchase system onto the website, but the website can be used as a bridge into the game, thus people can easily share avatars from their store listings outside of vrchat, without a user having to manually search it.",
